$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{12x^3+12x^2}{x^4-x^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{12x^2(x+1)}{x^2(x+1)(x-1)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{12\cancel {x^2}\cancel{(x+1)}}{{\cancel {x^2}\cancel{(x+1)}(x-1)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{12}{x-1}, \text{ for }x\neq 0,-1
\end{align}$
